  "id": "Compound::DB01236 - Gene::338567",
  "verbalization": "Sevoflurane, a commonly used anesthetic agent, is linked to Kcnk18 through a series of molecular interactions that involve anesthetic compounds and their binding to ion channels. The evidence suggests that Sevoflurane, as part of the anesthetic class, binds to Kcnk18, with the lowest common ancestor of Sevoflurane and its related compounds, such as Desflurane, being an organofluorine compound. This indicates a shared structural or functional relationship between Sevoflurane and other anesthetic agents. Additionally, Sevoflurane is associated with the development of Breath Holding Attacks, which are caused by Isoflurane, further reinforcing the role of anesthetic agents in triggering physiological responses. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Sevoflurane interacts with Kcnk18, likely through shared anesthetic properties and molecular binding, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
